        523.48095703125,
        286.9283447265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which predicts σsim,q",
      "bbox": [
        89.60900115966797,
        287.2877502441406,
        183.9750213623047,
        300.2433776855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "s0",
      "bbox": [
        165.4630126953125,
        294.0147399902344,
        173.0313262939453,
        301.8126525878906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "directly based on the initial state s0. This model is also used to compute",
      "bbox": [
        187.80099487304688,
        290.55609130859375,
        521.9224243164062,
        301.3092041015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "surrogate flowpipes for the trajectory segments ¯Xq, q ∈[N], representing the image of set I",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        301.3470764160156,
        521.199462890625,
        314.8581848144531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "through the model Fq(I ; θq).",
      "bbox": [
        90.00003051757812,
        317.0431823730469,
        230.7019500732422,
        328.4071960449219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Here are the reasons why this new training strategy for the trajectory σsim",
      "bbox": [
        106.93599700927734,
        329.2837219238281,
        450.36102294921875,
        340.8903503417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "s0 resolves all the",
      "bbox": [
        437.9750061035156,
        331.25762939453125,
        521.9763793945312,
        344.6943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "scalability issues, we listed for Hashemi et al. (2024b), in the Introduction section. First and",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        344.806640625,
        521.838134765625,
        354.4393615722656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "foremost, since all surrogate models Fq(s0 ; θq), q ∈[N] are directly connected to the initial",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        357.690185546875,
        521.9559936523438,
        369.6253662109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "state, we do not need to iterate them sequentially over the time horizon for prediction of states",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        371.9056396484375,
        521.9022216796875,
        381.5383605957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in σsim,q",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        382.13275146484375,
        127.55699920654297,
        395.0873718261719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "s0",
      "bbox": [
        109.04598999023438,
        388.8587646484375,
        116.61430358886719,
        396.65667724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ", q ∈[N], thus eliminating the problem of cumulative errors over the time horizon.",
      "bbox": [
        128.3459930419922,
        384.7891845703125,
        524.0006713867188,
        395.0873718261719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Furthermore in this setting, the size of the models Fq(s0 ; θq), q ∈[N] can be small. The small",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        398.3381652832031,
        521.9501342773438,
        410.2723388671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "size of the models allows for efficient computation of surrogate flowpipes ¯Xq := Fq(I ; θq)",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        409.7410888671875,
        523.2774658203125,
        423.8223571777344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for each segment via exact-star reachability analysis4. Additionally, the smaller models",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        424.1686096191406,
        521.9160766601562,
        435.734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fq(s0 ; θq), q ∈[N] enable efficient training of accurate models for each trajectory segment.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        438.9861755371094,
        524.0343627929688,
        450.92034912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Furthermore, although we have to train more models using this technique, we can train them",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        453.2006530761719,
        521.870361328125,
        462.8333740234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in parallel as they are totally independent processes.",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        466.7496337890625,
        339.37109375,
        476.3823547363281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the surrogate flowpipes ¯Xq = ⟨¯cq, ¯V q, ¯Pq⟩, for q ∈[N], are obtained as star sets,",
      "bbox": [
        106.93599700927734,
        477.4870910644531,
        523.46435546875,
        491.568359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the surrogate flowpipe for the entire trajectory forms another star set, ¯X = ⟨¯c, ¯V , ¯P⟩. This",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        491.03607177734375,
        521.9805297851562,
        503.4803771972656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "global surrogate flowpipe is constructed by concatenating all individual star sets ¯Xq, for",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        504.5850830078125,
        522.1973876953125,
        518.09619140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "q ∈[N], which implies: ¯c =",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        522.7881469726562,
        219.56028747558594,
        533.0863647460938
      ],
      "direction": [
